      "rev_n_5_098278_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_098278_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_098278",
        "thought_text": "The condition `if C % B == 0:` is incorrect because it checks if C is a multiple of B, not if it is congruent to C modulo B. The correct condition should be `if (C % B) % (A % B) == 0:`, which checks if the remainder of C divided by B is itself a multiple of the remainder of A divided by B. This ensures that the sum of selected multiples of A will be congruent to C modulo B.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6279941340635853406",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_098278_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_993cf18c26",
        "created_at": 1794527460.3783157
      },
      "rev_n_4_ac4cbf_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_ac4cbf_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_ac4cbf",
        "thought_text": "Instead of checking if C is a multiple of A, consider checking if there exists a combination of multiples of A that sum to a value congruent to C modulo B. This involves considering the properties of modular arithmetic and the constraints given.",
