      "rev_n_11_6546ed_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_6546ed_1",
        "node_id": "n_11_6546ed",
        "thought_text": "Instead of using the Chinese Remainder Theorem, let's focus on a simpler approach. We can check if there exists a non-negative integer k such that k * A ≡ C (mod B). This is equivalent to checking if A * k ≡ C (mod B) for some k. We can solve this by iterating through possible values of k and checking if we find a solution.",
